buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"eBay Inc., together with its subsidiaries, operates marketplace platforms that connect buyers and sellers in the United States, the United Kingdom, China, Germany, and internationally. Its marketplace platform includes its online marketplace at ebay.com, off-platform businesses, and the eBay suite of mobile apps. The company's platforms enable users to list, sell, buy, and pay various products. The company was founded in 1995 and is headquartered in San Jose, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jamie J. Iannone | CEO, President & Director | Age 52 | Compensation: $4.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 12K people. Revenue per employee of $902K ranks in the top quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $117K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $49K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["eBay Inc. is a large-cap consumer cyclical business with a $50.7B market cap on $11.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years and +3% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 18% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 9-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat. Gross margins of 72% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $1.4B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 13 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.96\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 9.3\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 5.7% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 10% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 2.6\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 315% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":3.148121734813316},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $16.7M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Widening credit spreads suggest growing stress in corporate debt markets","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Broad market in a downtrend, trading below its 200-day average","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Multiple macro indicators signal economic contraction","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 13% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Gross margin tops the Consumer Cyclical peer set \u2014 genuine pricing power is present here","Consumer Cyclical sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 5% over 3 months"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"(EBAY) Movement Within Algorithmic Entry Frameworks","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/132/EBAY_Movement_Within_Algorithmic_Entry_Frameworks_111826051002_1795039802.html","date":"2026-11-18","timestamp":1795039802.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"$100 Invested In eBay 15 Years Ago Would Be Worth This Much Today","source":"benzinga.com","link":"https://www.benzinga.com/news/26/11/63326542/100-invested-ebay-15-years-ago-would-be-worth-much-today","date":"2026-11-16","timestamp":1794867322.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.226,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Stock Market Today, Nov. 20: Amazon Shares Slide on AI and Mega-Cap Tech Sell-Off","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/stock-market-today-nov-20-225002397.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795215002.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.7,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Robinhood Markets vs. PayPal: Which Financial Stock Is a Better Buy for 2027?","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/robinhood-markets-vs-paypal-financial-120101000.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795176329.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.686,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"An Umbrella Girl Hummel Sold for $800 in 2000. Auction Houses Now Get About $100, and the Kids Who Inherit the Collection Get No Tax Break for the Drop","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/real-estate/articles/umbrella-girl-hummel-sold-800-080740740.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795162060.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.103,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[